WEBVTT

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:02.350
Well, let's get crackin'.

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:03.580
Let's-a-go.

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:05.920
Stop messing around and start!

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:35.590
Summer time!

00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:36.420
Beach time!

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:41.970
So Teacher and Cousin Yui are in
charge of supervising and driving today.

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:42.930
Gotcha!

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:44.370
But you know...

00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:46.760
The two of you have a lot of free time.

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:55.020
Sorry to impose on your day off.

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:55.610
It's nothing.

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:57.230
Don't sweat it.

00:01:57.230 --> 00:01:58.360
Narumi-san...

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:01.200
You're an officer in the
traffic safety department, right?

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.320
That's right.

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:04.280
I know all there is to know about traffic law.

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:06.740
He passed me.

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:08.500
Bastard...

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:08.870
<i>Wa-</i>

00:02:08.870 --> 00:02:09.540
<i>Hey!</i>

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:10.960
<i>What happened to safety first?</i>

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:14.040
Cousin Yui goes wild once her hand's on the stick.

00:02:14.210 --> 00:02:17.230
Guess we'll have to sacrifice Kagami and Tsukasa.

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:18.800
Really...

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:20.470
Isn't she a cop?

00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:21.670
Huh?

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:22.340
That's odd.

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:24.050
I lost sight of them.

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:27.630
Teacher, that's the wrong way!

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:29.100
That's a one-way street!

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:31.980
<i>I messed up big time!</i>

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:34.310
<i>I didn't expect them both to fail!</i>

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:56.960
That car's incredible!

00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:57.960
Who is it?!

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:00.170
They both have perfect braking and drifting!

00:03:00.170 --> 00:03:02.090
It's practically on top of the FDI!

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:03.840
And it's got better acceleration!

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:06.390
It's practically touching the guard rail!

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:08.350
The point of attack will come...

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:11.850
...in the five consecutive hairpin curves ahead!

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:18.560
It's speeding up!

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:20.150
Did the brakes die?!

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:26.530
Incredible!

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:31.190
What's with the (bleep) D-like driving?!

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:35.670
Nanako-san...

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:37.250
You're really good...

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:38.460
...at driving...

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:41.090
Yeah?

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:42.130
You see...

00:03:42.130 --> 00:03:44.960
I get sick whenever I'm in a car.

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:49.300
That's why I brought medicine...

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:53.930
But I didn't feel sick at all with you at the wheel.

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:56.940
Like!

00:03:57.270 --> 00:04:00.150
I don't have time to be talking to you!

00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:17.000
Well...

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:18.610
How about we find a hotel?

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:30.260
The clear sky is perfect weather for a day at the beach.

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:31.010
Seriously...

00:04:31.010 --> 00:04:33.310
I was getting worried there yesterday.

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:36.100
I'll put on my swimsuit before we go!

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:39.100
You're such a child...!

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:39.980
<i>Konata-san!</i>

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:41.770
<i>Are you seriously wearing that?</i>

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:42.570
And like...

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:45.780
I've never heard of someone
wearing a school swimsuit at this age.

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:48.280
Some people have special needs, Kagamin.

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:49.280
Izumi
Izumi

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:52.030
<i>H-H-How old is that swimsuit?!</i>

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:55.040
Besides...

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:58.460
Why are you wearing a swim ring
when you're good at sports stuff?

00:04:58.460 --> 00:05:02.540
The ocean doesn't exist solely
for wasting effort on swimming.

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:04.420
You should take it leisurely.

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:06.050
Leisure time.

00:05:06.050 --> 00:05:08.130
Plus, to meet those special needs...

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:11.470
...you have to wear a school swimsuit with a swim ring.

00:05:11.470 --> 00:05:12.930
People with special needs...

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:14.840
...won't be coming to the beach.

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:22.150
Watermelon cracking is the
usual event in manga and anime...

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:24.070
...but it doesn't happen much in reality.

00:05:24.070 --> 00:05:26.400
I've seen it before...

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:28.320
...but people probably feel like it's a waste.

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:29.700
That's true...

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:32.070
If you blow up a watermelon with a gun...

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:34.200
...you'll end up covered in watermelon.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:35.490
You watch too much anime.

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:37.540
Have you ever played it before, Miyuki-san?

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:38.870
Since you're rich.

00:05:38.870 --> 00:05:40.790
I haven't.

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:42.580
Well, on second thought...

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:45.840
It doesn't seem like something rich people would do.

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:47.580
You have a point.

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:56.390
It was obvious...

00:05:56.390 --> 00:05:58.890
...but I guess your eyes don't end up like in manga.

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:01.190
I'm sorry to disappoint you.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:03.230
But y'know, yeah?

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:07.070
A girls' only babysitting trip to the beach at this age...

00:06:07.070 --> 00:06:09.650
We're some lonely, single girls, huh?

00:06:09.650 --> 00:06:10.150
You're mistak-

00:06:10.150 --> 00:06:11.240
But yeah...

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:14.410
If the alternative is resorting to
bringing something like that...

00:06:14.410 --> 00:06:16.530
...I'm all for a girls' only trip.

00:06:16.530 --> 00:06:17.030
No, I'm...

00:06:17.030 --> 00:06:17.410
They're telling people to marry late these days.
No, I'm...

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:19.790
They're telling people to marry late these days.

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:22.960
Might as well take our time and choose well.

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:24.130
<i>You're mistaken.</i>

00:06:24.130 --> 00:06:26.710
<i>My husband just happens to be busy working far away.</i>

00:06:26.710 --> 00:06:28.480
<i>I'm already married!</i>

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:30.970
The beach is a mecca for flirting...

00:06:30.970 --> 00:06:33.220
...but it doesn't apply to us, huh?

00:06:33.220 --> 00:06:35.550
Well, it's less annoying this way.

00:06:36.140 --> 00:06:37.100
Besides, this thing...

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:40.680
...probably makes people think
we're sisters here with our parents.

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:46.610
And a oopsie-daisy.

00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:55.650
Wazzup?

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:57.160
Well...

00:06:57.160 --> 00:07:00.630
It kind of feels icky to sit down when I'm still wet.

00:07:00.910 --> 00:07:01.830
I understand how you feel.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:04.460
Then you can use an air chair.

00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:05.830
You're pretty extreme.

00:07:11.590 --> 00:07:12.470
What is it?

00:07:12.470 --> 00:07:13.590
My neck's tired.

00:07:13.590 --> 00:07:14.680
Really now.

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:17.430
Just as expected!

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:19.430
What are you so happy about?

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:22.930
Because I got something straight
out of a storybook beach house.

00:07:22.930 --> 00:07:24.600
Look at how the curry is sauce and nothing else.

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:26.190
This is true beach house fare!

00:07:26.190 --> 00:07:27.360
That's true.

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:30.110
Usually, you wouldn't be willing
to eat something like this...

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:33.530
...but here, it actually tastes good!

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:40.530
The beer they got at the beach is the best!

00:07:40.870 --> 00:07:43.500
Generic beer isn't too bad once in a while.

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:47.880
I find it odd that they're charging
300 yen for a single frankfurter.

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:48.920
Yeah!

00:07:48.920 --> 00:07:50.460
Maybe they're only half-cooked.

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:51.800
But we'll eat it anyway.

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:54.510
I actually like how their chicken is...

00:07:54.510 --> 00:07:58.090
...dripping in grease and over-spiced.

00:07:58.220 --> 00:08:00.180
And this plain fried soba...

00:08:00.180 --> 00:08:01.720
...is quite nice.

00:08:01.720 --> 00:08:02.930
But still...

00:08:02.930 --> 00:08:06.770
You couldn't stand eating this stuff at home!

00:08:07.850 --> 00:08:09.230
Konata's touched.

00:08:12.270 --> 00:08:13.150
Hey.

00:08:13.690 --> 00:08:15.740
Does this food really warrant so much praise?

00:08:15.920 --> 00:08:16.840
Not really.

00:08:16.840 --> 00:08:19.740
Not enough to make you run
towards the ocean in a loincloth.

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:21.990
Is that another anime reference?

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:31.750
Drank too much...

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:32.590
No choice.

00:08:32.590 --> 00:08:33.840
Let's stay another night.

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:35.720
What about work, Cousin Yui?

00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:37.470
I also took tomorrow off.

00:08:37.470 --> 00:08:38.690
It's fine!

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:45.980
I-It's freezing...

00:08:46.850 --> 00:08:49.170
You're such a kidder, Teacher.

00:09:20.430 --> 00:09:22.600
Why is your hair all squeaky...

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:24.720
...after you've been in the ocean?

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:25.470
Dunno.

00:09:25.470 --> 00:09:28.180
Maybe it has to do with salt or something?

00:09:28.180 --> 00:09:29.310
Right, Miyuki?

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:31.310
That's right.

00:09:31.310 --> 00:09:34.610
The main reason would be salt content and UV rays.

00:09:34.610 --> 00:09:36.820
What's so bad about it?

00:09:36.820 --> 00:09:39.860
Isn't your hair always getting hit by UV rays?

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:40.820
Well...

00:09:40.820 --> 00:09:43.030
It'll take a little while...

00:09:43.030 --> 00:09:45.120
...to explain that.

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:47.340
In that case...

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:52.540
The reason your hair is
damaged by a trip to the beach...

00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:55.840
...would be the adhesion of salt
from seawater and the sea breeze...

00:09:55.840 --> 00:09:58.050
...which absorbs the moisture from your hair...

00:09:58.050 --> 00:10:01.260
...which now suffers from exposure to strong UV rays.

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:01.970
Also...

00:10:01.970 --> 00:10:04.180
Whenever you are exposed
to strong UV rays outdoors...

00:10:04.180 --> 00:10:06.060
...your melanin levels will fade...

00:10:06.060 --> 00:10:08.660
...and your hair will become light brown.

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:12.190
And if residual quantities of
salt or chlorine remain in your hair...

00:10:12.190 --> 00:10:16.270
...they may result in the discoloration of your hair.

00:10:16.270 --> 00:10:18.730
The usual reason for hair damage in summer...

00:10:18.730 --> 00:10:21.490
...would be UV rays and residual substances.

00:10:21.490 --> 00:10:25.910
The above factors cause damage to the cuticles.

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:27.620
When exposed to strong UV rays...

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:31.960
...the cysteine molecules found
in strong hair are broken up...

00:10:33.580 --> 00:10:35.080
Look! Look!

00:10:35.210 --> 00:10:39.800
Timotei!

00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:41.300
What's that?

00:10:47.300 --> 00:10:51.050
I wonder how other people would see us.

00:10:51.480 --> 00:10:52.750
Not sure...

00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:58.730
<i>Nothing to talk about...</i>

00:10:59.900 --> 00:11:04.030
Probably sisters or cousins?

00:11:04.030 --> 00:11:05.240
Probably.

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:08.450
<i>That's all you have to say?</i>

00:11:08.450 --> 00:11:09.950
Cousin Yui!

00:11:09.950 --> 00:11:14.290
Timotei!

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:15.830
I remember that!

00:11:15.830 --> 00:11:16.710
I used to do it!

00:11:16.710 --> 00:11:17.460
Yes!

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:19.710
That's the response I wanted!

00:11:19.710 --> 00:11:21.380
How old are you?

00:11:24.430 --> 00:11:25.260
Mandom!

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:27.180
Cut out the geezer jokes.

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:28.800
What's wrong, Kona-chan?

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:30.640
I just triggered a flag.

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:31.930
What are you talking about?

00:11:31.930 --> 00:11:33.930
This is where the event starts!

00:11:33.930 --> 00:11:36.520
In order to see both paths...

00:11:36.520 --> 00:11:38.230
...don't forget to save often before a split!

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:39.860
No exceptions!

00:11:42.530 --> 00:11:43.690
Picture complete.

00:11:46.990 --> 00:11:47.870
Perfect!

00:11:47.870 --> 00:11:48.450
Bring it on!

00:11:48.450 --> 00:11:49.850
No idea what's going on.

00:11:50.490 --> 00:11:51.540
Anyway...

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:53.790
...you being like this is why...

00:11:53.790 --> 00:11:54.870
Why...?

00:11:54.870 --> 00:11:57.040
Why nobody came to hit on us.

00:11:58.750 --> 00:12:02.170
Y-You're the one who brought it up in the first place!

00:12:02.170 --> 00:12:05.880
I could really care less about that stuff.

00:12:06.590 --> 00:12:10.090
So Kagami wanted someone to hit on her.

00:12:10.090 --> 00:12:11.180
N-No...

00:12:11.180 --> 00:12:12.390
No!

00:12:13.640 --> 00:12:14.430
Phooey!

00:12:14.430 --> 00:12:16.060
I missed it!

00:12:20.900 --> 00:12:21.950
What is it?

00:12:23.570 --> 00:12:27.090
I was wondering what you do about hair.

00:12:27.090 --> 00:12:30.630
I'm pretty smooth so I don't do anything.

00:12:31.780 --> 00:12:32.790
What about you, Sis?

00:12:32.790 --> 00:12:34.120
M-Me?!

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:36.340
I guess I'm normal.

00:12:45.590 --> 00:12:48.880
Actually, today was kinda dangerous.

00:12:49.340 --> 00:12:50.260
What?

00:12:50.260 --> 00:12:51.930
Well...

00:12:51.930 --> 00:12:53.260
You know...

00:12:53.260 --> 00:12:54.680
Almost happened...

00:12:55.600 --> 00:12:56.640
Oh, that?

00:12:56.640 --> 00:12:57.060
I see.

00:12:57.060 --> 00:12:58.100
Good thing then.

00:12:58.480 --> 00:13:00.250
You were okay?

00:13:00.560 --> 00:13:01.900
No problem at all.

00:13:01.900 --> 00:13:03.480
Mine ended a week ago.

00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:05.940
The timing was perfect.

00:13:06.240 --> 00:13:08.450
It really sucks when that happens.

00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:09.950
You're right.

00:13:10.210 --> 00:13:12.830
It would be sad if you were the
only one who couldn't go in the water...

00:13:12.830 --> 00:13:15.120
But using that would be a little...

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:16.040
Yeah.

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:17.290
Makes you think twice.

00:13:17.290 --> 00:13:19.080
I've never used one.

00:13:20.870 --> 00:13:23.090
That was a candid conversation.

00:13:23.090 --> 00:13:25.090
Wh-What about you?

00:13:26.170 --> 00:13:27.460
Don't tell me...

00:13:27.460 --> 00:13:28.840
What's with that look?

00:13:28.840 --> 00:13:29.910
Nothing.

00:13:30.470 --> 00:13:33.890
Apparently, this is a true story...

00:13:35.060 --> 00:13:37.930
A photo software wholesaler...

00:13:37.930 --> 00:13:40.100
...was on his way home from work...

00:13:40.100 --> 00:13:43.770
...and got on the bus as usual late at night...

00:13:44.150 --> 00:13:45.860
His house was...

00:13:45.860 --> 00:13:48.860
...at the end of the bus line.

00:13:48.860 --> 00:13:49.570
So...

00:13:49.570 --> 00:13:52.410
As more and more passengers got off...

00:13:53.240 --> 00:13:57.830
...eventually, he was the only person left on the bus...

00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:04.810
The driver thought that nobody was left on the bus...

00:14:05.460 --> 00:14:06.340
...and...

00:14:08.300 --> 00:14:12.380
...sang "DANZEN! Futari wa ***Cure"
at the top of his lungs!

00:14:15.100 --> 00:14:17.220
Just a rumor I heard.

00:14:17.220 --> 00:14:19.250
It was nothing...

00:14:44.540 --> 00:14:45.580
What a relief...

00:14:45.580 --> 00:14:47.640
I was so scared.

00:14:48.420 --> 00:14:49.630
I'm also...

00:14:49.630 --> 00:14:50.630
I'm Sukekiyo.

00:14:54.220 --> 00:14:56.140
Where'd you get that mask from?!

00:14:56.300 --> 00:14:57.680
Then good night.

00:14:57.680 --> 00:14:58.100
Yes.

00:14:58.100 --> 00:14:59.600
Good night.

00:14:59.600 --> 00:15:00.470
The Inugami Family!

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:04.730
It's so much fun to scare you.

00:15:04.730 --> 00:15:06.190
Go to sleep already.

00:15:12.360 --> 00:15:13.070
Hey!

00:15:13.070 --> 00:15:14.280
We're going!

00:15:14.660 --> 00:15:15.570
Okay!

00:15:49.900 --> 00:15:53.280
<i>I don't have anything funny to say.</i>

00:15:56.450 --> 00:15:59.670
<i>I'm Tsukasa.</i>

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:13.130
Sis!

00:16:13.130 --> 00:16:14.130
What is it?

00:16:14.130 --> 00:16:14.550
I was scared!

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:19.010
A girl just took a step towards
becoming an adult, Kagamin.

00:16:22.310 --> 00:16:25.060
Comp Festival is a big hit.

00:16:25.060 --> 00:16:28.020
'Cause Japanese people are
suckers for limited edition stuff.

00:16:28.230 --> 00:16:30.860
If the words "limited edition"
are enough to boost sales...

00:16:30.860 --> 00:16:32.820
...they could just add it to everything.

00:16:33.190 --> 00:16:35.780
That would cheapen the value.

00:16:35.780 --> 00:16:38.160
So I went and asked.

00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:38.880
Yes.

00:16:38.880 --> 00:16:42.740
Clean your room before break's over.

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:47.540
Whoa, flashback!

00:16:47.540 --> 00:16:49.210
These textbooks are from middle school.

00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:50.250
Sis!

00:16:50.250 --> 00:16:51.840
Look at this album!

00:16:52.630 --> 00:16:54.380
Isn't this picture of Dad a little risqué?

00:16:54.380 --> 00:16:55.050
Right?

00:16:55.050 --> 00:16:58.300
That's when I started wondering about Dad's thing.

00:16:58.470 --> 00:16:59.470
You look like you're having fun...

00:16:59.470 --> 00:17:01.250
...but are you getting any cleaning done?

00:17:02.260 --> 00:17:04.640
Um...

00:17:04.640 --> 00:17:05.220
Hey.

00:17:05.220 --> 00:17:06.810
Do you want these clothes?

00:17:07.420 --> 00:17:08.980
If you don't need them, I'll take them.

00:17:08.980 --> 00:17:10.270
Then I'll leave them here.

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:11.990
Thanks.

00:17:14.210 --> 00:17:14.730
Hey.

00:17:14.730 --> 00:17:15.740
Do you want this?

00:17:16.150 --> 00:17:17.610
Then I guess I'll take it.

00:17:17.790 --> 00:17:19.030
What about this?

00:17:19.030 --> 00:17:19.820
This?

00:17:19.990 --> 00:17:20.660
<i>Wait!</i>

00:17:20.660 --> 00:17:23.700
<i>Don't tell me I'm her trash can...</i>

00:17:23.950 --> 00:17:26.930
You end up looking through
photo albums and stuff instead.

00:17:27.250 --> 00:17:28.330
I know what you mean.

00:17:28.330 --> 00:17:31.040
If any old magazines are
lying around, I start reading them.

00:17:31.040 --> 00:17:32.750
That's right.

00:17:32.750 --> 00:17:34.210
Oh, yeah. What about Tsukasa?

00:17:34.210 --> 00:17:38.050
She doesn't throw anything away so it takes a while.

00:17:38.050 --> 00:17:39.220
She's still at it.

00:17:39.800 --> 00:17:42.490
Tsukasa's always slow to act.

00:17:42.490 --> 00:17:45.220
On the other hand, Kagami's always trigger happy.

00:17:45.220 --> 00:17:47.850
Why is your impression of me...

00:17:47.850 --> 00:17:49.730
...so aggressive?

00:17:50.640 --> 00:17:53.230
You saved your textbooks from middle school.

00:17:53.520 --> 00:17:55.230
You don't have anything like that?

00:17:55.440 --> 00:17:59.320
I left them with my memories at my old school.

00:17:59.320 --> 00:18:00.820
No, take them home.

00:18:00.820 --> 00:18:02.570
You're causing trouble for the school.

00:18:03.320 --> 00:18:05.490
I finally finished cleaning.

00:18:06.030 --> 00:18:08.160
I think that I'll never use this again...

00:18:08.160 --> 00:18:10.330
...but then I remember how I just used it...

00:18:10.330 --> 00:18:12.040
...so I can't throw it away.

00:18:12.040 --> 00:18:12.620
Yeah.

00:18:12.620 --> 00:18:15.440
There really are people who keep everything.

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:17.420
Tsukasa seems the type.

00:18:17.590 --> 00:18:20.670
You seem like someone who
even throws away useful stuff.

00:18:20.670 --> 00:18:22.850
Seeing as how you ditched your textbooks.

00:18:23.840 --> 00:18:24.890
Miyuki.

00:18:24.890 --> 00:18:26.570
Go have your teeth taken care of...

00:18:26.570 --> 00:18:28.550
...before school starts up again.

00:18:28.550 --> 00:18:30.730
I understand...

00:18:30.730 --> 00:18:32.360
...but I just don't like it.

00:18:33.950 --> 00:18:37.640
Well, I would feel bad about forcing you to go.

00:18:38.280 --> 00:18:39.280
If you can't go...

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:40.360
...I'll have him come.

00:18:40.360 --> 00:18:41.360
A visit from the dentist.

00:18:41.360 --> 00:18:43.030
P-Please wait!

00:18:48.620 --> 00:18:50.410
Good lucky!

00:18:50.410 --> 00:18:54.040
We've already burst into the
sixth episode of Lucky Channel!

00:18:54.300 --> 00:18:58.210
I hope that you've all become familiar with this corner.

00:18:58.210 --> 00:18:59.610
I'm Akira Kogami!

00:19:00.840 --> 00:19:01.530
Lame!

00:19:01.970 --> 00:19:03.430
You say something?

00:19:04.970 --> 00:19:07.350
It appears that newbie Shiraishi-kun
isn't used to the job and a nervous wreck.

00:19:07.350 --> 00:19:08.720
I'm scared...

00:19:08.720 --> 00:19:09.010
You're all making his heart race.

00:19:09.010 --> 00:19:11.180
What did I do wrong?

00:19:11.180 --> 00:19:11.600
We went to the mountains 'cause Akira-sama said so.
You're all making his heart race.

00:19:11.600 --> 00:19:13.140
I hope he gets used to the job soon.

00:19:13.140 --> 00:19:13.690
Yeah.

00:19:13.690 --> 00:19:13.980
Went to the beach, too.

00:19:13.980 --> 00:19:14.850
And he better watch how he talks to the
veterans around here or else something may happen.

00:19:14.850 --> 00:19:18.730
I'm doing everything I can to make this show funnier!

00:19:18.730 --> 00:19:19.480
Yeah...

00:19:19.480 --> 00:19:19.940
The gum was hard...

00:19:19.940 --> 00:19:20.940
I just hate that!

00:19:20.940 --> 00:19:21.940
But it was fifty-four pieces.

00:19:21.940 --> 00:19:22.190
Today we'll introduce a key Lucky Star character...

00:19:22.190 --> 00:19:24.200
Fifty-four pieces in my mouth!

00:19:24.200 --> 00:19:24.650
But I still worked hard!
Today we'll introduce a key Lucky Star character...

00:19:24.650 --> 00:19:26.030
Konata Izumi-san!
But I still worked hard!

00:19:26.030 --> 00:19:28.000
What else will I have to do?
Konata Izumi-san!

00:19:29.330 --> 00:19:29.620
Hey.

00:19:29.620 --> 00:19:30.040
Stop blubbering.

00:19:30.040 --> 00:19:32.120
Why me?!

00:19:32.700 --> 00:19:33.580
Let's see...

00:19:33.580 --> 00:19:34.540
Konata Izumi-san.

00:19:34.540 --> 00:19:35.370
Seventeen years old.

00:19:35.370 --> 00:19:37.580
Her hobbies are gaming, watching anime, and reading.

00:19:37.850 --> 00:19:38.500
Uh...

00:19:38.500 --> 00:19:39.670
According to the data...

00:19:39.670 --> 00:19:42.210
...she always checks out new shows and books.

00:19:42.210 --> 00:19:45.010
She games up a storm on weekends.

00:19:45.150 --> 00:19:46.840
So she's a geek.

00:19:46.970 --> 00:19:47.720
Uh...

00:19:47.720 --> 00:19:49.010
Looks like it...

00:19:50.100 --> 00:19:51.280
<i>Come up with something quick!</i>

00:19:51.520 --> 00:19:53.020
By geek, you mean that, right?

00:19:53.020 --> 00:19:54.310
People who watch House Classics, right?

00:19:54.310 --> 00:19:57.020
The ones who watch A Dog of Flanders and cry, right?

00:19:57.940 --> 00:20:00.650
Which decade of geek are you talking about?

00:20:00.650 --> 00:20:02.360
Are you doing your homework?!

00:20:02.360 --> 00:20:04.240
Get with the program!

00:20:04.240 --> 00:20:05.700
N-No, uh...

00:20:05.990 --> 00:20:11.910
Well I guess A Dog of Flanders had the
whole cutesy, appealing character to soothe you.

00:20:11.910 --> 00:20:14.910
But people these days prefer a girl like me!

00:20:14.910 --> 00:20:17.540
Cute as a button and pure as snow!

00:20:17.540 --> 00:20:18.460
You know what I mean?

00:20:18.690 --> 00:20:20.830
If I look right, so do you!

00:20:20.830 --> 00:20:22.630
If I look left, so do you!

00:20:22.630 --> 00:20:25.800
When you line up for my concert the
night before, you can't take a shower!

00:20:25.800 --> 00:20:27.760
That may cause hygienic problems...

00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:29.300
...but you still want to see me!

00:20:29.300 --> 00:20:34.390
That determination burns as hot
as the sun in wait of my arrival!

00:20:34.390 --> 00:20:38.660
Until the bandana around your head is drenched!

00:20:42.070 --> 00:20:43.110
You know...

00:20:43.110 --> 00:20:45.490
They're still customers.

00:20:45.490 --> 00:20:49.410
When I'm doing handshakes
afterward, they won't stop talking.

00:20:49.410 --> 00:20:52.330
Yapping away during MC without reading the crowd.

00:20:52.330 --> 00:20:54.870
Doesn't that just blow?

00:20:55.580 --> 00:20:58.580
I'm only here because of them.

00:20:58.580 --> 00:21:01.920
I have to work hard for them.

00:21:01.920 --> 00:21:02.920
Y'know?

00:21:02.920 --> 00:21:05.170
Is that how it is...

00:21:05.170 --> 00:21:07.260
You'll know soon enough.

00:21:07.260 --> 00:21:09.630
How hard it is to be an idol...

00:21:09.630 --> 00:21:13.430
Once you've been through the
good and bad, you'll see how it really is.

00:21:13.430 --> 00:21:16.180
Can't do anything about fans or clients you hate...

00:21:16.890 --> 00:21:18.020
Perfect timing!

00:21:18.370 --> 00:21:19.140
Hey, everybody!

00:21:19.140 --> 00:21:21.560
Do you know who Konata-san is now?

00:21:21.560 --> 00:21:24.690
Then we'll see you on next week's Lucky Channel!

00:21:24.690 --> 00:21:26.150
Bye-bee!

00:21:27.190 --> 00:21:27.820
Uh...

00:21:27.820 --> 00:21:29.360
You didn't even introduce Konata...

00:21:29.360 --> 00:21:31.260
More like you introduced geeks.

00:21:31.990 --> 00:21:32.700
A-Akira-sama?

00:21:32.700 --> 00:21:33.830
You okay?

00:21:33.830 --> 00:21:34.620
Do it.

00:21:35.370 --> 00:21:36.200
Understood!

00:21:36.200 --> 00:21:38.120
What the correspondent saw then was...

00:21:38.120 --> 00:21:39.000
Not funny.

00:21:43.790 --> 00:21:45.960
Kage sure is awesome.

00:21:45.960 --> 00:21:47.800
We get the idea.

00:21:47.800 --> 00:21:49.480
So did you order a song, Tsukasa?

00:21:49.840 --> 00:21:50.760
I did.

00:21:50.760 --> 00:21:53.400
Tsukasa-san't singing is quite refreshing.

00:21:54.390 --> 00:21:56.100
I wonder if I can sing it well.

00:21:56.810 --> 00:21:58.490
What are you going to sing, Miyuki?

00:21:58.490 --> 00:22:01.100
I really don't know many songs...

00:22:01.100 --> 00:22:02.310
It's quite embarrassing.

00:22:05.500 --> 00:22:07.150
So she went with this, huh?

00:22:07.150 --> 00:22:08.870
Go for it, Tsukasa-san!

00:22:24.330 --> 00:22:25.590
Who's that?

00:22:35.300 --> 00:22:36.930
So who is she already?!

00:22:47.650 --> 00:22:48.980
Shut up already!

00:23:10.960 --> 00:23:13.170
Well, next time on Lucky Star:

00:23:13.590 --> 00:23:14.380
I'm Kagami.

00:23:14.950 --> 00:23:17.180
When you try to get rid of a hangnail...

00:23:17.180 --> 00:23:18.180
...and give it a little tug...

00:23:18.180 --> 00:23:19.720
...but then you end up pulling off too much...

00:23:19.720 --> 00:23:21.980
...it really hurts, doesn't it?

00:23:21.980 --> 00:23:22.810
Also...

00:23:22.810 --> 00:23:24.520
...there's the timing for ripping off a scab.

00:23:24.520 --> 00:23:25.590
When it starts to itch...

00:23:25.590 --> 00:23:26.690
...and you're thinking that it's about time...

00:23:26.690 --> 00:23:28.860
...so you pick it off bit by bit.

00:23:28.860 --> 00:23:31.520
And just when you're like everything is good...

00:23:31.520 --> 00:23:33.060
...it still ends up bleeding!

00:23:33.060 --> 00:23:35.230
It leaves some serious damage.

00:23:35.230 --> 00:23:36.010
Next time:

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:36.950
Image.

00:23:36.950 --> 00:23:38.490
Look forward to next time!
